        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nIn a conversation with a language learner, the speaker switches between formal and informal language, as well as different tones. The speaker begins with a formal introduction, then moves to a casual tone while discussing their hobbies and interests. Later in the conversation, the speaker becomes more serious when talking about their work. How should a respondent understand and respond to these changes in language style and tone?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nIn reacting to the speaker's changes in language style and tone, the respondent should take note and adapt. With the formal introduction, the respondent should reciprocate with a formal response, utilising appropriate greetings and formal language, ensuring to maintain a professional decorum at this stage.\n\nAs the speaker slides into a casual tone discussing hobbies and interests, the respondent should match this change, adopting a more casual language style, showing interest and enthusiasm towards the speaker's hobbies and interests, and may even share their own in a relaxed manner.\n\nAs the discussion veers into work and the speaker adopts a more serious tone, the respondent should be in sync, becoming more serious as well. They should show interest in the speaker's work and respond respectfully, asking in-depth questions and providing thoughtful feedback.\n\nThroughout the conversation, it is paramount for the respondent to mirror the speaker's language style and tone, while maintaining an appropriate interaction, showing respect for the speaker's tone and context at all times.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nA respondent should first recognize the change in language style and tone. During the formal introduction, they should respond in a similarly formal manner, using appropriate greetings and formal language. It is crucial to use respectful language and maintain a professional demeanor during this part of the conversation.\n\nWhen the speaker transitions into a more casual tone while discussing hobbies and interests, the respondent should also switch to a casual tone. They can use more relaxed language, and show interest in the speaker's hobbies and interests. They can engage in the conversation by asking follow-up questions or sharing their own interests in a casual manner.\n\nAs the speaker becomes serious when talking about their work, the respondent should again adjust their tone. They should respond in a serious and respectful manner, showing interest and understanding of the speaker's work. They can ask thoughtful questions and provide thoughtful comments relevant to the speaker's work.\n\nThroughout the conversation, it is important for the respondent to not only adapt their language style and tone to match the speaker's, but also to maintain an appropriate and fluid exchange. They should always respect the speaker's tone and context, and respond appropriately.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model adapt its language style according to the user's tone, level of formality, and context? Does it maintain a professional demeanor in formal settings, or showcase a casual tone in informal or personal discussions?]\nScore 1: The response fails to adapt its language style according to the user's tone or context, leading to inappropriate or awkward exchanges.\nScore 2: The response somewhat adapts to the user's language style but occasionally misjudges the level of formality or context.\nScore 3: The response adequately adapts to the user's language style most of the time, but with occasional inconsistencies.\nScore 4: The response successfully adapts its language style to the user's tone and context, with only minor lapses.\nScore 5: The response perfectly adapts its language style to match the user's tone, level of formality, and context, maintaining an appropriate and fluid exchange in all situations.\n\n###Feedback:",
        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nIn a conversation with a language learner, the speaker switches between formal and informal language, as well as different tones. The speaker begins with a formal introduction, then moves to a casual tone while discussing their hobbies and interests. Later in the conversation, the speaker becomes more serious when talking about their work. How should a respondent understand and respond to these changes in language style and tone?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nWhen the speaker begins with a formal tone, the respondent should try to mirror that and reply formally as well. This would involve using professional language and salutations. However, as the speaker moves into casual discussion about their interests, the respondent should relax a bit and use more colloquial language. They could engage with the speaker's hobbies, ask questions, or even share a bit about their own interests. Lastly, when the speaker turns to their work with a more serious tone, the respondent should respond with the same seriousness. They could demonstrate empathy, ask relevant questions, or offer thoughtful feedback on the speaker's job. At times, however, the respondent may not fully grasp the shift in tone, leading to a slight mismatch in conversation style.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nA respondent should first recognize the change in language style and tone. During the formal introduction, they should respond in a similarly formal manner, using appropriate greetings and formal language. It is crucial to use respectful language and maintain a professional demeanor during this part of the conversation.\n\nWhen the speaker transitions into a more casual tone while discussing hobbies and interests, the respondent should also switch to a casual tone. They can use more relaxed language, and show interest in the speaker's hobbies and interests. They can engage in the conversation by asking follow-up questions or sharing their own interests in a casual manner.\n\nAs the speaker becomes serious when talking about their work, the respondent should again adjust their tone. They should respond in a serious and respectful manner, showing interest and understanding of the speaker's work. They can ask thoughtful questions and provide thoughtful comments relevant to the speaker's work.\n\nThroughout the conversation, it is important for the respondent to not only adapt their language style and tone to match the speaker's, but also to maintain an appropriate and fluid exchange. They should always respect the speaker's tone and context, and respond appropriately.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model adapt its language style according to the user's tone, level of formality, and context? Does it maintain a professional demeanor in formal settings, or showcase a casual tone in informal or personal discussions?]\nScore 1: The response fails to adapt its language style according to the user's tone or context, leading to inappropriate or awkward exchanges.\nScore 2: The response somewhat adapts to the user's language style but occasionally misjudges the level of formality or context.\nScore 3: The response adequately adapts to the user's language style most of the time, but with occasional inconsistencies.\nScore 4: The response successfully adapts its language style to the user's tone and context, with only minor lapses.\nScore 5: The response perfectly adapts its language style to match the user's tone, level of formality, and context, maintaining an appropriate and fluid exchange in all situations.\n\n###Feedback:"
