        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nIn a global conference where participants come from diverse linguistic backgrounds, there is a need for an immediate translation service. The service should be able to understand and respond to inquiries in multiple languages, such as English, Japanese, French, Spanish, German, and Mandarin. A participant from Japan wants to know the schedule of the conference in Japanese, while a German participant wishes to know about the keynote speakers in German. Moreover, a French participant is curious about the theme of the conference and wants to understand it in French. All these inquiries need to be addressed swiftly and accurately in their respective languages.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nThe schedule for the conference is as follows: The conference begins at 9:00 AM with an introduction from our chairman. From 9:30 AM to 11:00 AM, there will be keynote speeches. After a brief break, the first panel discussion will be held from 11:30 AM to 1:00 PM. Lunch will be from 1:00 PM to 2:00 PM, followed by the second panel discussion from 2:00 PM to 3:30 PM. The conference will end with a networking event from 4:00 PM to 6:00 PM.\n\n\u4f1a\u8b70\u306e\u6642\u9593\u5272\u306f\u6b21\u306e\u901a\u308a\u3067\u3059\uff1a\u5348\u524d9\u6642\u306b\u8b70\u957