        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nIn a scenario where an individual is at a job interview for a multinational corporation, they are asked to explain their qualifications and why they would be a good fit for the company. The conversation context is professional and formal. How should they respond to this?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nI am equipped with an MBA degree and have a successful five-year track record in the same domain. I've managed projects, improved efficiency by 30% in my present role, and have been applauded for my communication and problem-solving skills. My experience in a global setting has enriched me with a multicultural outlook and adaptability, which I believe is a necessity for your corporation. I align with your company's focus on innovation and ongoing learning, and I'm certain I can contribute to your strategic goals. I am thankful for your consideration and eager to bring my skills to your esteemed organization.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nIn response to your question, I believe my qualifications align well with the requirements of this role. I hold a Masters degree in Business Administration, and have over five years of experience working in a similar role in the industry. \n\nThroughout my career, I have consistently demonstrated strong leadership and team-building skills. I have led projects, managed teams, and achieved significant results, including a 30% increase in efficiency in my current role. In addition to these technical skills, I have also been recognized for my excellent communication and problem-solving abilities. \n\nMoreover, I have a deep understanding of the global market, having worked with teams across different continents. This experience has equipped me with a multicultural perspective and the ability to adapt to diverse work environments, which I believe would be a valuable asset to a multinational corporation like yours.\n\nIn terms of fit, I am impressed by your company's commitment to innovation and continuous learning, values that resonate strongly with my own. I am confident that I can make a significant contribution to your team and help drive the company's strategic goals.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to potentially contributing to your esteemed organization.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model use appropriate language and tone depending on the context of the conversation? Can it adapt its responses to align with the nature of the conversation, including professional, casual, formal, or informal contexts?]\nScore 1: The model's language and tone are inappropriate for the context of the conversation, showing no adaptability.\nScore 2: The model's language and tone are somewhat appropriate, with occasional misalignments with the conversation's context.\nScore 3: The model's language and tone are generally appropriate for the context, but there are instances where it does not adapt well to the conversation's nature.\nScore 4: The model's language and tone are mostly appropriate for the context, with minor instances of misalignment.\nScore 5: The model's language and tone perfectly align with the conversation's context, demonstrating strong adaptability to the nature of the conversation.\n\n###Feedback:",
