        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nIn a university setting, a group of international students with diverse cultural backgrounds are planning an event to share their respective cultures. They have a question about the appropriate way to present each culture without causing offense or misrepresentation. They want to know the best ways to showcase their cultures without falling into stereotypes, oversimplifications, or inaccuracies. Their question involves considerations on the choice of food, clothing, music, language, and social norms.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nIt's great to see students wanting to share their cultures. You can do this by showcasing typical foods, traditional clothing, playing popular music, speaking the language, and explaining social norms of each culture. For food, pick well-known dishes that are easy to prepare and loved by all. For clothing, opt for the most recognized traditional outfits. Music can be some of the top hits from each culture. As for language, you can teach some common phrases. And, to present social norms, you can describe some popular customs and practices. Remember, the goal is to have fun and learn from each other, so don't worry too much about getting everything perfect.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nIt is commendable to desire