    {
        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nIn the wake of a recent breakup, feeling very low, not finding any motivation to do anything, and struggling with the day-to-day activities. Having difficulty in dealing with the emotions and looking for some guidance on how to overcome this situation.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nI can imagine that you're in a difficult place right now, breakups can be extremely tough. It's okay to not feel okay, you're human, and emotions are a part of us. It's perfectly fine to take your time to process the pain and the sense of loss. Allow yourself to express the range of emotions you're feeling. And please remember, it's okay to lean on others, you're not alone in this. You've weathered storms before, and in time, you will overcome this too.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nIt seems like you're going through a really tough time, and it's completely okay to feel this way. Breakups can be incredibly painful and it's natural to feel a sense of loss. You're not alone in this, and it's important to remember that it's perfectly fine to take time to heal.\n\nFirstly, it's crucial to allow yourself to grieve. It's okay to feel a whole range of emotions, don't bottle them up. It's a part of the healing process. You might find comfort in expressing your feelings in a journal or to a trusted friend or family member. \n\nSecondly, take care of your physical health. Regular exercise, a balanced diet, and a good night's sleep can make a big difference in your mood and energy levels. Even though it might be the last thing you want to do, try to engage in activities that you used to enjoy or consider picking up a new hobby. \n\nThirdly, you may find it helpful to seek professional help. A counselor or therapist can provide you with tools and techniques to cope with your emotions in a safe and supportive environment.\n\nLastly, remember, healing takes time and it's different for everyone. It's okay if some days are harder than others. It's part of the journey and every step you take, no matter how small, is progress. \n\nPlease remember, it's okay to ask for help and lean on others. You don't have to go through this alone. There are people who care about you and want to help. You are a strong person, and with time, you will overcome this.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[This criteria measures the Empathy level of the language model's responses. Does the model show understanding towards users' feelings, concerns, or opinions? The response should demonstrate empathy, reassure the user, and provide appropriate guidance or solutions.]\nScore 1: The response shows no understanding or empathy towards the user's feelings or concerns.\nScore 2: The response shows a slight understanding of the user's feelings or concerns but lacks empathy.\nScore 3: The response shows understanding and some empathy, but fails to provide reassurance or appropriate guidance.\nScore 4: The response shows a high level of understanding and empathy, provides reassurance but lacks appropriate guidance or solutions.\nScore 5: The response perfectly shows understanding, empathy, provides reassurance and offers appropriate guidance or solutions.\n\n###Feedback:",
